{
  "_": [
    "iron_maiden_le on Team Hackjob + VPW's 'Iron Maiden Legacy of the Beast' (Original 2022) 1.0.12,",
    "built on JPSalas' Mago de Oz: a scripted tribute, kept as a shadow game. Despite 'Original' it",
    "is a close recreation of Stern's Iron Maiden LE playfield (the Pro has no Underworld eject, no",
    "up/down ramp and no Sarcophagus lock, which this table has), so the LE card is the one it",
    "takes. Placement was fitted to the rig's switch_xy.txt (16 anchor pairs, residuals under 30",
    "units over the lower two thirds) and to led_io.txt (LED drawing -> table: x*3.36-48,",
    "y*3.35-35, every insert within a few units); the top of the drawing is compressed, so the",
    "back-of-table switches were decided by what their hit subs do.",
    "NOT driven: the Sarcophagus lock (Ramp Motor CPU Unload/Load/Unload/Flat 94-97) and the",
    "Guardian diverter (Diverter Motor Up/Down 76/77) are MOTORS the game runs through LED-driver",
    "outputs (node 9 LEDs 56-61), which the bridge cannot see; the table's own lock and Guardian",
    "stay where its init leaves them (Guardian closed), so the lock is unreachable and Top Ball",
    "Sense (79) is never made.",
    "Numbers: switch 1000+id (switch_list.txt), solenoids the small numbers under `solenoids`;",
    "flippers keep core.vbs's 46/48 and 36 (up left) / 34 (up right)."
  ],
  "title": "iron_maiden_le",
  "model": "LE",
